From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herrie <Github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 8 Aug 2026 17:47:55 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add groups.d definition for the media.pipeline ACG

com.webos.sim-pipeline.api.json maps the com.webos.pipeline.* control
APIs to the media.pipeline access control group, but no groups.d file
declares that group, so it only exists implicitly:

WARNING: luneos-dev-image-1.0-r0 do_validate_ls2_acg: Found 2 group(s) that appear only in api-permissions.d, consider define them in groups.d
=== LIST BEGIN: Groups used in api-permissions.d but not defined in groups.d ===
  media.pipeline
=== LIST END ===

Declare it alongside the other pipeline groups, using the same trust
level ("oem") as com.webos.sim-pipeline.role.json.in.
Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 files/sysbus/com.webos.sim-pipeline.groups.json | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 files/sysbus/com.webos.sim-pipeline.groups.json

diff --git a/files/sysbus/com.webos.sim-pipeline.groups.json b/files/sysbus/com.webos.sim-pipeline.groups.json
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..526517e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/files/sysbus/com.webos.sim-pipeline.groups.json
@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@
+{
+    "allowedNames": [
+        "com.webos.pipeline.*"
+    ],
+    "media.pipeline": ["oem"]
+}
